Usage: seq [OPTION]... LAST
seq [OPTION]... FIRST LAST
seq [OPTION]... FIRST INCREMENT LAST

Print numbers from FIRST to LAST, in steps of INCREMENT.

OPTIONS:
  -f, --format ARG      use printf style floating-point FORMAT
  -s, --separator ARG   use STRING to separate numbers
  -t, --terminator ARG  use STRING to terminate the output instead of newline
  -w, --equal-width     equalize width by padding with leading zeroes
      --help            display this help and exit
  -V, --version         output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
